        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This should be resolved on latest `main`. There is no a third \"Cancel\" choice which stops synchronization altogether. The `synchronize()` now also returns boolean indicating whether synchronization was performed or not.\n\nI briefly considered to simply repurpose \"No\" choice to also stop synchronization, but it somewhat goes against documented `synchronize()` [purpose](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/f90b6b820062fc06d6d51ed61a0f9b7f9a13b01b/doc/mini-files.txt#L754-L755): it is not *only* about making user's edits to file system, but also about synchronizing explorer's content with what is actually on disk. That way \"No\" choice indeed is reasonable to treat as \"skip applying user's changes and just sync with disk\".",
            "created_at": "2025-01-23T09:59:06Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1439#issuecomment-2609372341",
